<title>SPAIN: Endesa shares welcome Retevision bid news.</title>
<headline>Endesa shares welcome Retevision bid news.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Spanish electrical group Empresa Nacional de Electricidad (Endesa) outpaced the market on Monday, welcoming news it was in a consortium to bid for the privatisation of 60 percent of Retevision.</p>
<p>&quot;The news was expected and confirms Endesa's intentions,&quot; said a banking analyst.</p>
<p>At 1015 GMT, Endesa was up 130 pesetas, or 1.38 percent, to 9,580 pesetas, while the IBEX index of 35 leading shares was up just 29.23 points, or 0.53 percent, to 5,659.40.</p>
<p>Earlier today, Italian state-controlled telecoms group STET said it had agreed a co-operation telecoms deal with Endesa and Union Fenosa to take part in a privatisation bid for Spain's second telephone operator, Retevision.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
